WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.800
Meet TraceRook, a native Mac companion for reviewing risky coding agent
actions.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:14.800
The dashboard brings sessions, findings, and pending reviews together. This
walkthrough uses labeled demo data, with no real commands executing.

3
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:23.800
Open a session to see the task and its timeline. Here, the sample shows a
credential upload blocked by local policy.

4
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:33.800
Each finding explains the proposed action, its evidence, and its relationship
to your task. Local rules retain authority over critical denials.

5
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:43.800
Higher-risk actions can wait for your review. The native panel shows the task,
evidence, exact action binding, and a deadline.

6
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:53.800
Choose Block and the simulated review resolves immediately. Allow once applies
to one exact action; the coding agent still controls its own permissions.

7
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:59.800
TraceRook Cloud uses Anthropic Claude. Explore the invited Mac beta at
tracerook.dev.
